        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "cc473ae8-d982-56ae-bc96-fc89c179380a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: Korean War, Battle of Mindanao\n- Places: Korea, Mindanao, Philippines\n- Countries: North Korea, South Korea, China, Soviet Union, United States, Japan\n- Organizations: Filipino guerrillas\n- Operations: Operation VICTOR V\n- People: Claire E. Hutchin, Jr.\n- Awards: Distinguished Service Cross\n\nFacts:\n- The Battle of Mindanao was fought on the island of Mindanao in the Philippines from 10 March 1945 to 15 August 1945 by United States forces and allied Filipino guerrillas against Japan, and the actions were officially designated Operation VICTOR V.\n- The Korean War lasted from 25 June 1950 to 27 July 1953 and was fought between North Korea and South Korea.\n- China and the Soviet Union supported North Korea during the Korean War.\n- The United States was the principal supporter of South Korea during the Korean War.\n- Claire E. Hutchin, Jr. received two Distinguished Service Crosses during the Korean War.",
